# Live credentials — never committed
references/.env_keys
*.env
*.env.*

# Not a credential: version pins interpolated into build.args (01.2 SF-2).
# Committed intentionally so the smoke check can assert it agrees with
# docs/records/agent-verification.md.
!compose/pins.env

# SF-2 fixture scratch (throwaway PKI, proxy logs, agent workspaces)
.build-scratch/

# Generated trust material (01.3 SF-3). mediator/identity/ carries its own
# deny-all .gitignore; this is the second line of defence, so a private key
# cannot be committed by someone working from the repository root who has not
# read that file.
mediator/identity/ca/
mediator/identity/listeners/
mediator/identity/clients/
# 01.6 SF-3. Proxy credentials: per-agent PLAINTEXT and the htpasswd the mediator verifies
# against. `*.key` and `*.pem` below do not cover these -- a `.cred` file is a bearer secret
# with no extension anyone would guess, which is exactly why it gets its own line.
mediator/identity/credentials/
*.key
*.pem

# The default profile's project mount (01.3 SF-4). The directory is committed
# via its .gitkeep so Docker does not auto-create it root-owned; its contents
# are the operator's scratch work and are never this repository's.
workspace/*
!workspace/.gitkeep

# The acceptance harness's throwaway fixture PKI (01.3 SF-8). Generated before every run and
# torn down with it; a self-signed certificate for `*.fixture.test` is not trust material
# anyone should be able to find in version control and mistake for the mediator's.
tests/fixtures/tls/

# Generated host-derived material (01.4 SF-1, R8.7). compose/generated/ carries its own
# deny-all .gitignore; this is the second line of defence, so the operator's scrubbed
# gitconfig cannot be committed by someone working from the repository root who has not read
# that file. The scrub removes credential.helper, but name, email and signing config are
# still the operator's personal configuration and still derived material regenerated before
# every `up`.
compose/generated/gitconfig.d/

# Agent credential material (01.4, R4.7/R8.7). None of this SHOULD reach the repository --
# OAuth credentials live on the per-agent state volumes and API keys arrive by environment --
# so every one of these patterns firing means something went wrong. They are here to make that
# mistake non-committable rather than to describe a normal layout.
#
# auth.json is Codex's OAuth credential file; .credentials.json is Claude Code's; .claude.json
# is the account record R4.4 places OUTSIDE CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The oauth-mount staging
# directory (SF-4) holds a copy of the host credential with OPENAI_API_KEY stripped, and is
# the one path here an operator is actually expected to create.
auth.json
.credentials.json
.claude.json
compose/generated/oauth-src/
